{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966804,"nonce":"qevVMnBPD4027r9PvuJY+2kKpAs=","title":"Text min-content measurement inflated flex-parent heights","message":"**Symptom:** `h_fit()` containers balloon to viewport size when they contain a `text()` child with wrap enabled (the default). Multiple sibling cards with identical structure but different text content end up with *different* heights. The card's layout-debug outline stays small but its painted background extends to the window edge because taffy's computed main-axis size is inflated.\n\n**Root cause pipeline:**\n\n1. `blinc_layout::tree::text_measure_function` (tree.rs:100-106) maps taffy's `AvailableSpace::MinContent` to `max_width: Some(0.0)` as a sentinel meaning \"wrap at every word\".\n2. `FontTextMeasurer::measure_with_options` (blinc_app/src/text_measurer.rs) forwarded that `Some(0.0)` straight to `blinc_text::LayoutEngine::layout` alongside `LineBreakMode::Word`.\n3. `blinc_text` can't fit any word in zero pixels, so it falls back to breaking at every character. Result: returned height = `char_count × line_height` (20 chars × 15.6 ≈ 312 px, 23 chars ≈ 359 px).\n4. Taffy uses that inflated height as the text item's `hypothetical_outer_size` when collecting flex lines. The card's children exceed the parent's main-axis available space → `lines.len() \u003e 1`.\n5. `determine_container_main_size` (taffy-0.6.3 flexbox.rs:931) returns `f32_max(content, main_axis_available_space)` when `lines.len() \u003e 1` — so the card's auto main-axis size becomes `max(content, viewport_height)`, i.e. the whole window.\n\n**Fix:** in `FontTextMeasurer::measure_with_options`, detect `max_width \u003c= 0.0` and remap to the min-content width (widest word as measured with no wrap). Keeps words whole, keeps text ~18 px tall, keeps flex from inflating.\n\n**How this hid in unit tests:** `blinc_layout`'s unit tests never install `FontTextMeasurer` — they fall back to `EstimatedTextMeasurer`, which short-circuits `max_width \u003c= 0` at lines 189-194 in `text_measure.rs` by returning `(total_width, 1)`. So plain-div + text tests all pass; only real-app runs through `FontTextMeasurer` see the bug. Any future regression test for h_fit / flex-wrap / text interactions MUST install a real measurer.\n\n**Canonical repro:** two cards, `.flex_col().h_fit().flex_wrap().overflow_clip()`, each containing `text(\"Some Label\")` + `div().w(N).h(N)`. Without the fix: heights grow linearly with character count of the label. With the fix: both cards equal, sized to content.","files":null}]}